Three workers still ended in the same validation worker failure, confirming per-worker allocation—not aggregate concurrency—is the limiting factor. I’m adding a profiling-only validation batch size of four configurations. It preserves the exact candidate set, order, solver, and outputs, but intentionally makes validation more memory-bounded (and likely slower); normal production behavior remains untouched.
