--- /dev/null
+++ b/.scratch/cert-profile/spec.md
@@ -0,0 +1,16 @@
+# Certification timing diagnostic
+
+Completion criterion: one agent-runnable profiling command must emit at least
+20 deliberately tail-heavy, uncensored real-provider decisions.  Every row
+must contain monotonic `t_first`, `t_winner`, `t_certified`, and `t_total`
+offsets, an exclusive wall-time ledger that reconciles to `t_total`, candidate
+and oracle counts, and the identity of the eventual `FULL` winner.  The final
+report must give p50/p95/max for `t_certified - t_winner` beside `t_winner`,
+identify late-finding versus late-certification anchors, and discuss the
+threshold-aware requirements for a valid pruning bound without implementing
+one.
+
+This is `DIAGNOSTIC_NOT_CLAIM`.  No scientific parameter, budget, guard,
+threshold, seed, horizon, price, or acceptance rule may change.  The profiling
+run disables enforcement of the existing cutoff solely to observe the same
+reference procedure to completion.
